>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SDest`

``` hol4
clasetLib.SDest : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a safe destruction rule for one tactic invocation.

`SDest th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but carries a marker recognized
by classical tactics. The theorem is added to the call's temporary rule set
as a safe destruction rule. A destruction rule derives consequences from a
major premise matched against an assumption; it is converted internally to
elimination-rule form.

The argument-free `[sdest]` theorem attribute persistently registers the
same classification. The plain `[dest]` attribute and `Dest` marker denote
unsafe destruction rules. Per-invocation markers do not alter the stored
classical rule set.

### Failure

Constructing `SDest th` does not validate the rule. A tactic that consumes
the marker may fail if `th` has no suitable major premise or cannot be
converted from destruction-rule form to elimination-rule form.

### Example

``` hol4
classicalLib.CLARIFY_TAC [clasetLib.SDest my_dest_rule]
```

Here `my_dest_rule` is safe only for this tactic call.

